{"type":"message","id":"37cc6c33","parentId":"2a175a95","timestamp":"2026-06-02T00:04:48.555Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I can see the issue clearly:\n\n**ETH position:**\n- qty = 0.008 ETH\n- entry = $1998.41 \n- notional = $15.99 USDT (messed up!)\n- margin ≈ $1.6 USDT\n\nThis is way off. The config says 20 USDT margin per position (200 USDT notional at 10x). But ETH only has $1.60 margin ($15.99 notional). This is clearly wrong.\n\n**XRP position:**\n- qty = 9.5 XRP\n- entry = $1.2838\n- notional = $12.20 USDT\n- margin ≈ $1.22 USDT\n\nAlso way too small! Should be $200 notional at 10x ($20 margin).\n\n**DOT position:**\n- notional = $195.74 USDT → close to the correct $200\n\n**BTC position:**\n- notional = $219.76 USDT → close to correct $200\n\nSo the issue is clear: ETH and XRP positions are extremely under-sized. They should have notional around $200 but they have only ~$12-16. \n\nThe problem is likely in the quantity calculation in the auto-opening logic. Let me check how the monitor calculates position sizes.\n\nThe issue seems to be with the `format_quantity` function or the `get_quantity_precision` function. Let me check those.\n\nFor ETH at $1998, with $200 notional at 10x (20 USDT margin):\n- Quantity = 200 / 1998 = 0.1001 ETH ≈ 0.1 ETH\n\nBut actual position is 0.008 ETH. That's about 12-13x too small.\n\nFor XRP at $1.2838, with $200 notional at 10x (20 USDT margin):\n- Quantity = 200 / 1.2838 = 155.8 XRP\n\nBut actual position is 9.5 XRP. That's about 16x too small.\n\nSo the quantities are being calculated wrong. The actual amounts seem to be using margin ($20) as the notional, then dividing by price:\n- ETH: 20 / 1998 ≈ 0.01 ETH → 0.008 is close (maybe precision trimming)\n- XRP: 20 / 1.2838 ≈ 15.58 → 9.5 seems off...\n\nWait, let me recalculate. Actually, let me look at how the position opening works. The problem might be that when calculating quantity, it's using margin (20 USDT) instead of notional (200 USDT) as the base.\n\nActually: 20 / 1998 = 0.01001 → close to 0.008 (maybe some precision truncation)\n20 / 1.2838 = 15.58 → but actual is 9.5... hmm.\n\nActually the precision might be at play here. Let me just look at the auto_trade code to find where the quantity calculation happens.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"找到了老公。ETH 和 XRP 的开仓金额确实有问题："},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_SpdKNaxEObAWJ6JYJyKu5490","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/root/.openclaw/workspace/scripts/binance_auto_trade.py","offset":253,"limit":30}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":245,"output":1394,"cacheRead":27136,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":28775,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1780358677116}}
{"type":"message","id":"e6931600","parentId":"37cc6c33","timestamp":"2026-06-02T00:04:48.654Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_00_SpdKNaxEObAWJ6JYJyKu5490","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"def get_quantity_precision(symbol, price):\n    \"\"\"\n    根据 Binance API 的 stepSize 动态获取数量精度\n    来源：/fapi/v1/exchangeInfo LOT_SIZE.stepSize\n    \"\"\"\n    # 币种精度映射（仅保留当前交易的币种）\n    # 更新：2026-03-28 老公指示：添加 BTC\n    precision_map = {\n        'BTC': 3,      # stepSize: 0.001\n        'ETH': 3,      # stepSize: 0.001\n        'SOL': 2,      # stepSize: 0.01\n        'BNB': 2,      # stepSize: 0.01 ✅ 2026-03-28 修复：3→2 位\n        'DOT': 1,      # stepSize: 0.1\n        'LINK': 2,     # stepSize: 0.01\n        'XRP': 1,      # stepSize: 0.1 ✅ 2026-03-31 同步：加回 XRP\n    }\n    \n    return precision_map.get(symbol.upper(), 8)  # 默认 8 位\n\ndef format_quantity(symbol, quantity, price):\n    \"\"\"格式化数量到正确的精度（Binance 要求 8 位小数）\"\"\"\n    precision = get_quantity_precision(symbol, price)\n    \n    # 简单 round 到正确精度\n    # 修复：XRP 精度 1 位，8.5/2=4.25 → 4.2（向下兼容）\n    return round(quantity, precision)\n\ndef format_price(price):\n    \"\"\"格式化价格到正确的精度\"\"\"\n    if price >= 1000:\n\n[300 more lines in file. Use offset=283 to continue.]"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1780358688640}}
