{"type":"message","id":"75780585","parentId":"ec65d443","timestamp":"2026-06-02T00:06:21.701Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Something is odd - the algo orders all have `qty=None` and `price=0.000`. This seems like either a parsing issue or these are the stop-loss take-profit orders that are paired with positions. But the quantity should be set.\n\nLet me look more at this and also check the position sizes by comparing with the correct calculation. Let me also directly compute what the correct quantities should be and present the findings to the user.\n\nLet me verify by directly calling the formula:","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_pW8TzabTnm4njOeZziu82448","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"python3 -c \"\n# Simulate the formula\ntotal_capital = 100\nsize_pct = 0.20\nleverage = 10\n\neth_price = 1998.41\nxrp_price = 1.2838\n\neth_raw = (total_capital * size_pct * leverage) / eth_price\nxrp_raw = (total_capital * size_pct * leverage) / xrp_price\n\neth_formatted = round(eth_raw, 3)\nxrp_formatted = round(xrp_raw, 1)\n\nprint(f'ETH: raw={eth_raw:.6f} → formatted={eth_formatted} → notional={eth_formatted * eth_price:.2f} USDT')\nprint(f'XRP: raw={xrp_raw:.6f} → formatted={xrp_formatted} → notional={xrp_formatted * xrp_price:.2f} USDT')\nprint()\nprint('Actual positions:')\nprint(f'ETH: qty=0.008 → notional={0.008 * eth_price:.2f} USDT (expected {eth_formatted * eth_price:.2f})')\nprint(f'XRP: qty=9.5 → notional={9.5 * xrp_price:.2f} USDT (expected {xrp_formatted * xrp_price:.2f})')\nprint()\nprint(f'ETH shortfall: {eth_formatted * eth_price - 0.008 * eth_price:.2f} USDT ({eth_formatted * eth_price / (0.008 * eth_price):.1f}x)')\nprint(f'XRP shortfall: {xrp_formatted * xrp_price - 9.5 * xrp_price:.2f} USDT ({xrp_formatted * xrp_price / (9.5 * xrp_price):.1f}x)')\n\"","timeout":5}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":502,"output