{"type":"message","id":"0d59883d","parentId":"e094f5c5","timestamp":"2026-06-02T00:08:25.961Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"`-2022 ReduceOnly Order is rejected` — this means the reduce-only order would increase the position rather than reduce it. For a LONG position, SELL should reduce it... unless the position doesn't actually exist anymore.\n\nWait, the XRP close already succeeded. Maybe the ETH position was also closed somehow? Let me check the current positions.\n\nActually, the error \"-2022 ReduceOnly Order is rejected\" happens when:\n1. The position doesn't exist (already closed or never existed)\n2. The order would increase the position instead of reducing it\n\nFor ETH, we have a LONG position of 0.008 ETH. A SELL 0.008 should reduce it. Unless the position was already closed by the previous attempt? Let me check...\n\nActually wait, the previous ETH close attempt returned `-4164 notional too small` but didn't actually place the order. So the position should still be there. Let me check current positions.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_pL8JCmQTqBlFYW0uT5zz4927","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd ~/.openclaw/workspace/scripts && python3 -c \"\nimport sys\nsys.path.insert(0, '.')\nimport importlib\nimport binance_auto_trade as bat\nimportlib.reload(bat)\n\n# Check current positions\npositions = bat.get_all_positions()\nfor p in positions:\n    print(f\\\"{p['symbol']} {p['type']} qty={p['amount']} entry={p['entry_price']} mark={p['current_price']} pnl={p['unrealized_pnl']}\\\")\n\" 2>&1 | grep -v InsecureRequestWarning | grep -v 'warnings\\.' | grep -v 'INFO.*加载'","timeout":15}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":197,"output":600,"cacheRead":43904,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":44701,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1780358898200}}
