{"type":"message","id":"7b7dfe3a","parentId":"0685a3de","timestamp":"2026-06-02T00:08:45.807Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"XRP is gone (closed successfully), ETH is still there. But the reduce_only SELL is being rejected with -2022.\n\nWait, -2022 \"ReduceOnly Order is rejected\" could mean the reduce_only order would create a new position in the opposite direction, but that doesn't make sense for SELL on a LONG position...\n\nOh wait, I think the issue might be with the quantity precision. The order is passing `0.008` as quantity, but the formatted quantity might be getting rounded differently. Let me check.\n\nActually, looking at the place_order function:\n```python\nformatted_quantity = format_quantity(symbol.replace(\"USDT\", \"\"), quantity, price) if price > 0 else quantity\n```\n\nFor ETH: format_quantity(\"ETH\", 0.008, 2004.0) = round(0.008, 3) = 0.008. That's fine.\n\nHmm, but Binance might reject it because the notional is still below minimum, even though reduce_only should bypass that. Let me check the Binance docs more carefully.\n\nActually, -2022 can also happen when the position doesn't exist or when the reduce_only order can't be matched against the current position. But we confirmed ETH LONG exists with 0.008.\n\nWait, maybe the issue is that Binance's reduce_only check is based on the order notional being too small (5 * 0.008 = notional of ~$16, Binance minimum is $5 or $10). Let me check...\n\nActually, maybe the problem is that even with reduce_only, there's still a minimum quantity requirement. Let me try without reduce_only but with the correct quantity.\n\nActually, let me try a different approach. Since the ETH position is only 0.008 (notional ~$16), I can't close it as a reduce_only order if the notional is below some Binance threshold. Let me close it by opening a SELL order that is NOT reduce_only, equal to the position size.\n\nWait, but a non-reduce_only SELL of 0.008 would create a short position instead of reducing the long. Not what we want.\n\nLet me try another approach - just close it with a MARKET SELL that opens a new short and then closes everything. Or better yet, let me just open the CORRECT position sizes on top:\n\n1. ETH currently has 0.008 LONG, need 0.1 LONG → open 0.092 additional LONG\n2. XRP already closed, need to open 155.8 LONG\n\nThis is actually cleaner. For ETH, instead of closing and reopening, I'll just add to the position.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"ETH 平不掉（reduce_only 还是被拒，可能是仓位太小达不到最低限额）。换个思路 — ETH 直接补仓到正确数量，XRP 重开。"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_rKZUkUZ2DgsJGpc4SWHV1439","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd ~/.openclaw/workspace/scripts && python3 -c \"\nimport sys\nsys.path.insert(0, '.')\nimport importlib\nimport binance_auto_trade as bat\nimportlib.reload(bat)\n\n# ETH: need 0.1 total, have 0.008 → buy 0.092 more\neth_buy = bat.place_order(\n    symbol='ETHUSDT',\n    side='BUY',\n    quantity=0.092,\n    leverage=10,\n    price=2004.0,\n    reduce_only=False\n)\nprint(f'ETH 补仓: success={eth_buy.get(\\\"success\\\")} msg={eth_buy.get(\\\"message\\\")}')\n\n# XRP: need 155.8 total, currently 0 → buy 155.8\nxrp_buy = bat.place_order(\n    symbol='XRPUSDT',\n    side='BUY',\n    quantity=155.8,\n    leverage=10,\n    price=1.295,\n    reduce_only=False\n)\nprint(f'XRP 开仓: success={xrp_buy.get(\\\"success\\\")} msg={xrp_buy.get(\\\"message\\\")}')\n\" 2>&1 | grep -v InsecureRequestWarning | grep -v 'warnings\\.' | grep -v 'INFO.*加载'","timeout":30}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":217,"output":1496,"cacheRead":44416,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":46129,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1780358909942}}
