{"type":"message","id":"6ddb1801","parentId":"aab8b280","timestamp":"2026-06-02T00:09:46.870Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"No runtime modifications to CONFIG. So the formula was 200/entry_price when the positions were opened.\n\nLet me reconsider. Maybe ETH and XRP were NOT opened by the `open_position` function. Maybe they were opened by some other code path.\n\nLet me search for any other place_order calls or order placement in the monitor:\n- Line 1066: open_position → place_order\n- Line 1176: close_position → place_order (reduce_only=True)\n\nSo there's only one way to open a position in the monitor. \n\nWait, maybe the issue is with the `quantity=round(qty, 6)` being passed to place_order. Let me check — `round(155.8, 6)` = 155.8. That's fine. `round(0.1001, 6)` = 0.1001. Then place_order would format it again.\n\nBut wait, in place_order:\n```python\nformatted_quantity = format_quantity(symbol.replace(\"USDT\", \"\"), quantity, price) if price > 0 else quantity\n```\n\nformat_quantity(\"ETH\", 0.1001, entry_price) = round(0.1001, 3) = 0.1. That's fine.\n\nformat_quantity(\"XRP\", 155.8, entry_price) = round(155.8, 1) = 155.8. That's fine.\n\nSo the quantities should be correct. Something else is happening.\n\nHmm, let me think about this from a completely different angle. What if the positions were actually correct at the time they were opened, but Binance partially filled them? Like, if the order was only partially filled?\n\nFor ETH: ordered 0.1, but only 0.008 filled. That's 8% fill rate — possible in a low-liquidity testnet environment.\nFor XRP: ordered 155.8, but only 9.5 filled. That's 6% fill rate.\n\nBut Binance testnet should have enough liquidity... Market orders should fill completely.\n\nActually wait, let me check if there was a Binance \"MIN_NOTIONAL\" filter being hit. The minimum notional for Binance futures is $5. 0.008 * 1998 = $16, above the minimum. And 0.1 * 1998 = $199.8, also above.\n\nLet me check another possibility: maybe there was an error during the order placement that caused a partial fill or a retry with smaller quantity.\n\nOr... maybe the positions were opened by a completely different mechanism. Let me check if there's any running process or scheduled task that might open positions.\n\nActually, let me just look at the monitor log to find when these positions were opened.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_ksQIQhZ8xIAAUnSWrG9c8936","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Check if there are log files from the running monitor\nfind /root/.openclaw/workspace -name '*.log' -newer /root/.openclaw/workspace/scripts/crypto_news.log 2>/dev/null | head -10\n# Also check tmp and var\nfind /tmp -name '*.log' -mmin -1440 2>/dev/null | head -10\nfind /var/log -name '*crypto*' 2>/dev/null | head -5\nfind /var/log -name '*monitor*' 2>/dev/null | head -5","timeout":5}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":45,"output":1337,"cacheRead":48256,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":49638,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1780358974011}}
